  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "This recipe uses 4 large and 4 mini food storage containers.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry the fresh produce.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 lime\n1 head butter (Boston) lettuce\n1 English cucumber\n1 small pkg fresh basil"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Juice lime into a small bowl.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel and mince garlic and shallots. Add both to the bowl with the lime juice along with oil, vinegar, fish sauce, and soy sauce, then stir to combine the dressing. Set aside.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "4 clove garlic\n¼ cup toasted sesame oil\n¼ cup rice vinegar\n¼ cup fish sauce\n¼ cup soy sauce"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a large skillet over medium-high heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add the pork and cook, breaking it apart with a spoon, until starting to brown, 3-4 minutes.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "680 g lean ground pork"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Add ⅓ of the dressing to the skillet and continue to cook, stirring occasionally, until the pork is cooked through and coated, 3-4 minutes more. Remove from heat and set aside to cool, 20 minutes. (Divide remaining dressing between the mini containers, cover, and set aside.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, separate lettuce into leaves. Divide between the large containers.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Trim and slice cucumber crosswise into thin rounds. Add to the containers with the lettuce.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Pick basil leaves off the stems; discard stems and add leaves to the containers.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Thinly slice chili peppers into rings; seed and remove ribs with a spoon to reduce spice level. Add to the containers. (Be careful with chilis; do not touch your eyes and ensure you wash your hands after handling or wear gloves while preparing.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Divide cooled pork between the containers, then add dressing. Cover and refrigerate until ready to eat. Fill lettuce leaves with pork, veggies, and dressing. Enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
